WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.336 --> 00:00:04.797
Here we are on the set of The Changeling.

00:00:04.797 --> 00:00:08.634
This is Kelly Marcel, showrunner and creator of The Changeling.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:12.596
And this is Victor LaValle, author of The Changeling novel.

00:00:12.596 --> 00:00:18.310
And we’re here at apartment 305, the home of Apollo and Emma, our heroic leads.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.019
Shall we go inside?

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:19.937
Let’s go.

00:00:21.647 --> 00:00:25.609
Here we are in baby Brian’s bedroom, the scene of the crime.

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:27.820
But before we get to those terrible things,

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.990
some of my favorite details include the curtain that hangs here

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:34.535
where you can see the motif of the forest coming in,

00:00:34.535 --> 00:00:38.038
so that you constantly feel like the outside world is&nbsp;creeping in,

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.039
and what’s creeping in with it.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.835
And all of these things become very important in Season 1.

00:00:42.835 --> 00:00:46.213
And then one of the other really magically things is this book.

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:48.257
To the Waters and the Wild.

00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:49.049
It’s a good one.

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:52.803
A little children’s book my father read to me.

00:00:52.803 --> 00:00:56.056
It tells a creepy but wonderful tale that we really appreciated.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.266
It was kind of incredible

00:00:57.266 --> 00:00:57.600
Yes.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.351
how spot on this book is

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:01.312
when we talk about the story of our show.

00:01:01.312 --> 00:01:02.229
Absolutely.

00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:04.148
The young one is gone,

00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:05.399
but they’ll never know.

00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:07.359
In its place, a thing without life,

00:01:07.359 --> 00:01:08.569
hard and cold.

00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:10.154
Where are you?

00:01:10.154 --> 00:01:11.822
Not a baby!

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.744
Why don’t we check Apollo and Emma’s bedroom now?

00:01:16.744 --> 00:01:17.578
Let’s do it.

00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:20.998
We have a few things here as well that speak to the themes of our show

00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:23.834
that have been planted by Lester,&nbsp;our production designer.

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:28.005
And it’s another place where Lester has brought the outside world in, so you’ll see

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:31.383
forests and boats.

00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:35.888
And as a little Easter egg, Apollo has a coat, inside that coat is a forest.

00:01:35.888 --> 00:01:41.268
The woods plays a very large part in the creeping dread of the tale.

00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:42.394
And there’s more forests over here.

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:46.565
And the fact that Apollo and Emma are sleeping under this painting

00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:51.987
only gains significance and power as&nbsp;you get to know more and more about what might be being suggested.

00:01:51.987 --> 00:01:53.781
We go here into the kitchen,

00:01:53.781 --> 00:01:58.244
a place of great horror in all the best ways.

00:02:03.749 --> 00:02:05.918
But it’s not only a place for hard times.

00:02:05.918 --> 00:02:11.173
One of the sweet details is that Emma is a real world traveler.

00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:15.928
And so some of these magnets are from some of the places where we imagine she had traveled to.

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:18.514
One of the places she goes to is Brazil.

00:02:18.514 --> 00:02:20.641
She brings magic back.

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:23.769
That magic has huge repercussions for everybody.

00:02:24.228 --> 00:02:26.981
People don’t just disappear.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.775
Tell me your life’s voyage.

00:02:32.611 --> 00:02:34.905
And I will tell you who you are.

